# Genuinely accepted findings only. Every entry needs a reason; do not add
# an entry to silence something that should instead be fixed.

# GCP-0017 (HIGH): "Database instance is granted a public internet
# address" -- gcp-cloud-run/sql.tf, google_sql_database_instance.this,
# ip_configuration.ipv4_enabled.
#
# Accepted: the instance has no authorized_networks entries (see the
# comment next to ip_configuration in sql.tf), so the public IP accepts no
# direct connections from an allowlisted CIDR. The only supported access
# path is Cloud Run's built-in unix-socket connector, which uses the Cloud
# SQL Auth Proxy over an IAM-authenticated, mutually authenticated TLS
# tunnel (roles/cloudsql.client on the calling service account, short-lived
# certificates) -- not the instance's declared IP. ssl_mode is
# ENCRYPTED_ONLY. Going private-IP-only would remove this finding but
# requires a VPC network, a reserved peering range and Direct VPC egress on
# every Cloud Run revision (service and init job); the module's requirement
# is only "no authorized networks", which is what this configures.
# Revisit if the module grows a VPC anyway for another reason.
AVD-GCP-0017

# Cloud Run public invoker binding (google_cloud_run_v2_service_iam_member.
# public_invoker, role roles/run.invoker, member allUsers) -- not currently
# flagged by this trivy checks bundle version (verified: a full severity
# scan finds no rule for it), but documented here anyway, since a future
# checks-bundle update may add one.
#
# Accepted: intentional. Authentication is OAuth 2.1 + OIDC login at the
# application layer (every /mcp call is checked against a verified
# Principal; /approve and /admin pages require a configured-approver OIDC
# login), not at the Cloud Run IAM layer. See
# docs/adr/0008-cloud-run-and-cloud-sql.md.
